================
Secure Management VLAN

Why we did this
================
By default, switch management traffic is often carried on the same VLAN used by normal users.

This creates several risks:

- Unauthorized access to switch management interfaces
- Increased attack surface
- Easier reconnaissance by attackers
- Exposure of SSH, SNMP and management services
- Difficulty applying management-specific security policies

Administrators wanted to separate management traffic from user traffic.

To achieve this, a dedicated Management VLAN is created exclusively for managing network devices.

This is known as a Secure Management VLAN.

What will happen
================
1. A dedicated VLAN is created for management.
2. Only administrators can access the management VLAN.
3. Switch management traffic is separated from user traffic.
4. SSH, SNMP and other management protocols use the Management VLAN.
5. User devices cannot directly access management interfaces.
6. Security and monitoring become easier.

