Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Separates management traffic from users.
2. Reduces attack surface.
3. Improves network security.
4. Easier ACL implementation.
5. Simplifies management monitoring.
6. Supports SSH, SNMP and Syslog security.
7. Follows security best practices.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Requires VLAN planning.
2. Requires proper routing configuration.
3. Additional administration required.
4. Misconfiguration may block management access.
5. Not a replacement for AAA or SSH security.

Hence what came next
--------------------
Even with a dedicated Management VLAN, attackers may still attempt to access the switch management plane.

Administrators needed to protect the management processes themselves.

This led to:

Management Plane Protection

which secures:
- SSH Access
- SNMP
- Management Services
- Administrative Access

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Create Management VLAN

Switch(config)# vlan 99
Switch(config-vlan)# name MANAGEMENT


Assign Management IP

Switch(config)# interface vlan 99
Switch(config-if)# ip address 192.168.99.2 255.255.255.0
Switch(config-if)# no shutdown


Configure Default Gateway

Switch(config)# ip default-gateway 192.168.99.1


Assign Uplink Port

Switch(config)# interface g0/1
Switch(config-if)# switchport mode trunk
Switch(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,30,99


(Optional ACL Protection)

Switch(config)# access-list 10 permit 192.168.99.0 0.0.0.255

Switch(config)# line vty 0 4
Switch(config-line)# access-class 10 in

Verification
============

show vlan brief

show ip interface brief

show interfaces trunk

show access-lists

